                                "sense_id": "6628e262-dcac-3298-b9b4-49717a3c05ad",
                                "text": "Those people coined the term “open source,” to stress the instrumental benefits of allowing others to scrutinize code: these scrutineers could root out defects and prevent the nefarious subversion of code to spy on or steal data from its users (there’s a saying for this, too: “with enough eyeballs, all bugs are shallow”)."
